Going to Expert for multi-fire is very powerful for missiles (dagger
in the case of Valk) but has far less value for melee.  It's a DevTeam
trap to try to get you to waste limited skill slots for melee weapons
compared to the power of #twoweapon.  Spending the slots early
means you can't #enhance other classes early.

For a Valk I tend to ramp up dagger to Expert ASAP mixed with
some effort to move long sword to Skilled.  I will only #enhance
war hammer once dagger is at Expert.  I value #twoweapon over
war hammer once I have Excalibur.  I save 2 slots for the 2 spell
skills slot when I'mmoving through the XP=21-29 range.

Dagger - Expert for the multi-fire
Long sword - Skilled for melee, think Excalibur or Frosty

Might exit mines at these skills.

Saber - To Skilled if I get Greyswandir
#twoweapon - to Skilled to match the primary Excal or Grey.
Hammer - To Skilled if I don't get Greyswandir before Medusa.
Attack spell - Basic for Cone of Cold - Rules at Medusa

Might hit Medusa at these skills.

All of those before any of the rest -

Polearm - To Skilled for the 2 castle gates with a knight's attack.

Except if I plan on using it for Ludios it gets moved earlier ...

Escape spell - Basic if jump comes available.
Pickaxe - Basic because the slot is available.
Other artifact gifts - Basic if I want.

Only then will I spend the slots on either long sword or hammer
to Expert.  Note that I value Mojo far less than many but that
would probably change if I started playing more neutral Valks.



